  "claim": "James Bridges co-wrote a script for a movie starring John Travolta. The script was parodied by the first country album by Alvin and the Chipmunks which covers the song Boot Scootin' Boogie.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Aaron Latham. Sentence: Aaron Latham (born October 3, 1943) is an American journalist who wrote the article that inspired the movie \"Urban Cowboy\" and co-wrote its script with director James Bridges.\nPage: Urban Cowboy. Sentence: It was John Travolta's third major acting role after \"Saturday Night Fever\" and \" Grease\".\nPage: Urban Chipmunk. Sentence: The title parodies the 1980 movie \"Urban Cowboy\".\nPage: Boot Scootin' Boogie. Sentence: Alvin and the Chipmunks released a cover, done in their signature style, for the 1993 re-release of \"Urban Chipmunk\".",
